<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?><alert xmlns="urn:oasis:names:tc:emergency:cap:1.2"><identifier>2625738456985519</identifier><sender>2625738456985519</sender><sent>2026-07-14T21:29:51-04:00</sent><status>Actual</status><msgType>Alert</msgType><scope>Public</scope><code>CAPSv1.2</code><info><language>en-US</language><category>Safety</category><event>Civil Emergency Message</event><urgency>Immediate</urgency><severity>Severe</severity><certainty>Observed</certainty><eventCode><valueName>SAME</valueName><value>CEM</value></eventCode><expires>2026-07-14T23:29:51-04:00</expires><senderName>NYCEM [English]</senderName><headline>Notify NYC - Canadian Wildfires Air Quality - 7/15 (NYC)</headline><description>Notification issued 07-14-2026 at 09:29 PM.

NYCEM and DOHMH are advising New Yorkers to prepare for potential deteriorating air quality from the Canadian wildfires beginning Wednesday, 7/15. Stay inside as much as possible when the Air Quality Index (AQI) is above 100 and stay in a cool space during periods of extreme heat. If you must be outside when air quality is poor, consider wearing a well-fitting KN95 or N95 mask to reduce inhalation of fine particulate matter. 

To protect the health of New Yorkers, especially those at greatest risk, free KN95 masks are available at public library branches across the five boroughs, including Brooklyn Public Library, Queens Public Library, and select New York Library locations. The City is working to expand availability at additional distribution sites and will announce further locations if air quality worsens. Stay hydrated &amp; seek medical attention if you experience severe difficulty breathing or chest pain.

For more information, visit: https://on.nyc.gov/4wHAwdq</description><parameter><valueName>timezone</valueName><value>EST</value></parameter><area><areaDesc>Bronx,Kings,New York,Queens,Staten Island</areaDesc><polygon>40.9191,-73.9082 40.9075,-73.8642 40.9168,-73.8489 40.8954,-73.8319 40.8752,-73.7679 40.8533,-73.7574 40.8275,-73.7827 40.8222,-73.7933 40.7882,-73.757 40.7909,-73.7418 40.7502,-73.6892 40.727,-73.6981 40.7207,-73.7138 40.7113,-73.7219 40.66,-73.7213 40.6443,-73.7206 40.6318,-73.7344 40.6232,-73.7576 40.6118,-73.7357 40.5866,-73.7332 40.5782,-73.7894 40.5641,-73.8479 40.5485,-73.9 40.5289,-73.9596 40.5597,-74.0093 40.5824,-74.0409 40.5838,-74.0631 40.5574,-74.0917 40.5262,-74.1303 40.5199,-74.1641 40.5083,-74.1869 40.4944,-74.2289 40.4939,-74.2552 40.5117,-74.2588 40.5287,-74.2483 40.5474,-74.2525 40.5604,-74.2332 40.5631,-74.2169 40.5898,-74.2094 40.6006,-74.2006 40.6041,-74.2053 40.6286,-74.2054 40.6483,-74.1826 40.6519,-74.1592 40.6471,-74.1182 40.6524,-74.0673 40.6919,-74.0544 40.7107,-74.035 40.735,-74.0216 40.7586,-74.0146 40.7907,-73.987 40.8255,-73.9653 40.8736,-73.9394 40.9191,-73.9082</polygon><geocode><valueName>SAME</valueName><value>036005</value></geocode><geocode><valueName>SAME</valueName><value>036047</value></geocode><geocode><valueName>SAME</valueName><value>036061</value></geocode><geocode><valueName>SAME</valueName><value>036081</value></geocode><geocode><valueName>SAME</valueName><value>036085</value></geocode></area></info></alert>